# GetApproachEngagePoses — given a StorageSystem-style (storage_id, slot)
# pair, derive the APPROACH and ENGAGE end-effector poses for that slot.
#
# storage_id follows the same convention as storage_system's node names:
# "eurocontainer_left", "eurocontainer_right", "redboard_left",
# "redboard_right" (kind = prefix before "_<side>", side = "left"/"right").
# Gripper storage is NOT covered here — an SPL "in gripper" has no
# APPROACH/ENGAGE motion of its own (see SPECS doc).
#
# slot is the same flat slot index used by StorageSystem for that
# storage_id (0-39 for eurocontainer, 0-7 for redboard).
#
# group_name / target_frame — control which frame the returned poses are
# expressed in (this node DOES look up TF and transform into this frame,
# see SPECS doc Decision #1 revised 2026-08-03):
#   - if target_frame is non-empty, it wins outright (explicit override).
#   - else if group_name is non-empty, it is resolved to a root frame via
#     the ~group_root_frames ROS param map (e.g. "left_arm" -> "yumi_base_link").
#   - else falls back to the node's ~default_root_frame param (default:
#     "world").
# Both fields may be left empty to just get the default root frame.

string storage_id
int32 slot
string group_name
string target_frame
---
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped approach_pose
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped engage_pose
bool success
string message
